{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Probability, Bayes, and Kalman Filter\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"Finding Truth in a Noisy World\"\n",
        "author: \"Christopher Reckner\"\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  revealjs: \n",
        "    auto-animate: true\n",
        "    auto-animate-easing: ease-in-out\n",
        "    auto-animate-duration: 1.0\n",
        "    theme: dark\n",
        "    transition: slide\n",
        "    transition-speed: default\n",
        "    slide-number: true\n",
        "    chalkboard: true\n",
        "    controls: true\n",
        "    progress: true\n",
        "    history: true\n",
        "    center: true\n",
        "    hash: true\n",
        "    width: 1920\n",
        "    height: 1080\n",
        "    margin: 0.1\n",
        "    \n",
        "    css: custom.css\n",
        "\n",
        "engine: jupyter\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 1: Agenda -->\n",
        "## Agenda {.center}\n",
        "\n",
        "### Timing Summary\n",
        "\n",
        "| Time | Section | Duration |\n",
        "|------|---------|----------|\n",
        "| 0:00 – 0:05 | Introduction | 5 min |\n",
        "| 0:05 – 0:35 | Part I: Logic of Maybe | 30 min |\n",
        "| 0:35 – 0:55 | Part II: Bayes Activity | 20 min |\n",
        "| 0:55 – 1:05 | BREAK | 10 min |\n",
        "| 1:05 – 1:30 | Part III: Gaussians | 25 min |\n",
        "| 1:30 – 1:55 | Part IV: Kalman | 25 min |\n",
        "| 1:55 – 2:00 | Conclusion | 5 min |\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 2: Introduction - The Hidden State -->\n",
        "## Introduction: The Hidden State {.left auto-animate=\"true\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.fragment  .fade-in}\n",
        "### Error is inescapable \n",
        "What is 5 cm truely? Can we ever measure a perfect 5cm?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.fragment  .fade-in}\n",
        "### Yes and No\n",
        "* To a drill press : 5cm => 5cm +- .5cm\n",
        "* To a mill : 5cm => 5cm +- .005cm\n",
        "* To an ASML Photolithography Machine: 5cm => 5cm +- 0.000002cm\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "::: {style=\"height: 5em;\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.fragment .goal-box .fade-up}\n",
        "### Today's Goal\n",
        "The Mathmatics of finding truth through Error, and incorporating new data as Evidence rather than truth. \n",
        "Since by definition we cannot measure the error of any particular measurment, We use probability to model the likelyhood of sensing a true value\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {style=\"height: 2em;\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Boolean vs. Probabilistic Logic\n",
        ":::{.columns}\n",
        ":::{.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "### Boolean Logic"
      ],
      "id": "91adebe3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "# Boolean logic example\n",
        "# if (Shooter_will_make_the_shot == True):\n",
        "#     shoot"
      ],
      "id": "f3af5f78",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "### Probabilistic Logic"
      ],
      "id": "e184bf6b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "# Probability logic example\n",
        "# if (Probability_we_make_the_shot >= 80%)\n",
        "#     shoot"
      ],
      "id": "0c8b7bfa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "### Key difference:\n",
        "Combining evidence with trust levels enables better decisions.\n",
        "\n",
        "* Boolean: Instantaneous sensor read → immediate judgment\n",
        "\n",
        "* Probabilistic: Averages sensor noise, reduces false positives/negatives\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "### Caveat:\n",
        "There are alternative filtering approaches that don't rely on probability:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Rolling average on distance sensors\n",
        "- Debounce period on limit switches  \n",
        "- Moving median filters\n",
        "- Exponential smoothing\n",
        "- These can work very well depending on implementation and use case\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "- We want a number that represents how often something happens, or does not\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "- If you know nothing about an event, you could assume it's a 50:50 chance, pass or fail, it will happen or it wont\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "- With Evidence about the type of event (I.E. Rolling a 2 on a D6 Die) you can refine your guess, in this case to 1:6\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "- You can also experiment to find probability. If given a weighted die, you could roll it many times to gather data, and hone in on the true likelyhood of any given face landing up. \n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 3: Understanding Set Space (Part 1) -->\n",
        "## Let's Visualize Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "For Example: We have ball shooter, and a scout finds that during competition we make our shot ~ 30 % of the time\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.clearfragment}\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: absolute; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box-label\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 700px; top: -20px;  color: #42affa; font-size: 50px;\">All Possible States: Balls Shot -- Our Set/Universe</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 200px; width: 700px; height: 700px; background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.3); border: 3px solid #ff6464; border-radius: 50%;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 900px; top: 250px; color: rgba(255, 100, 100, 1); font-size: 50px;\">Target Hit -- Our Event. The fraction of balls shot which made it to the target</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 4: Understanding Set Space (Part 2) -->\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "- The scout also notices that our shooter was broken for some part of the competition, and also collects that data. Suprisingly, we still made a few shots despite the mechanical failure. \n",
        "- Our set representation below uses area to show how often each event occured for all the shots we fired during\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box-label\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 700px; top: 40px;  color: #42affa; font-size: 50px;\">All Possible States: Balls Shot</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 200px; width: 700px; height: 700px; background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.3); border: 3px solid #ff6464; border-radius: 50%;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; color: white; font-size: 40px; \">$$P(\\text{Target Hit})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"circle2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 850px; top:350px; width: 240px; height: 240px; background: rgba(100, 255, 100, 0.3); border: 3px solid #64ff64; border-radius: 50%;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label2\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 900px; top: 200px; color: white; font-size: 30px; \">$$P(\\text{Shooter Was Broken})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 5: Understanding Set Space (Part 3 - AND) -->\n",
        "## What Can we Identify in our Set? {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "### Target Hit AND Shooter Was Broken\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box-label\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 700px; top: 40px; color: #42affa; font-size: 50px;\">All Possible States: Balls Shot</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Container for blend mode effect -->\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1500px; height: 880px; isolation: isolate;\">\n",
        "  <!-- Circle 1 - darker with blend mode -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 200px; width: 700px; height: 700px; background: rgba(134, 134, 134, 1); border: 0px solid #ff6464; border-radius: 50%; mix-blend-mode: overlay;\"></div>\n",
        "  \n",
        "  <!-- Circle 2 - darker with blend mode -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 850px; top: 350px; width: 240px; height: 240px; background: rgba(146, 146, 146, 1); border: 0px solid #64ff64; border-radius: 50%; mix-blend-mode: plus-lighter;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; color: white; font-size: 40px; \">$$P(\\text{Target Hit})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label2\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 900px; top: 200px; color: white; font-size: 30px;\">$$P(\\text{Shooter Was Broken})$$</div>\n",
        ":::{.clearfragment}\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 950px; top: 800px; color: #64ff64; font-size: 30px; font-weight: bold; text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px black;\">$$P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cap \\text{Shooter Broken})$$</div>\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 6: Understanding Set Space (Part 4 - OR) -->\n",
        "## What Can we Identify in our Set? {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "### Target Hit OR Shooter Was Broken\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box-label\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 700px; top: 40px; color: #42affa; font-size: 50px;\">All Possible States: Balls Shot</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Container for blend mode effect -->\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1500px; height: 880px; isolation: isolate;\">\n",
        "  <!-- Circle 1 - darker with blend mode -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 200px; width: 700px; height: 700px; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); border: 0px solid #ff6464; border-radius: 50%; mix-blend-mode: normal;\"></div>\n",
        "  \n",
        "  <!-- Circle 2 - darker with blend mode -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 850px; top: 350px; width: 240px; height: 240px; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); border: 0px solid #64ff64; border-radius: 50%; mix-blend-mode: normal;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; color: white; font-size: 40px; \">$$P(\\text{Target Hit})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 900px; top: 200px; color: white; font-size: 30px;\">$$P(\\text{Shooter Was Broken})$$</div>\n",
        ":::{.clearfragment}\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 950px; top: 650px; color: #64ff64; font-size: 30px; font-weight: bold; text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px black;\">$$P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cup \\text{Shooter Broken})$$</div>\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 7: Understanding Set Space (Part 5 - NEITHER) -->\n",
        "## What Can we Identify in our Set? {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "### Neither Target Hit NOR Shooter Was Broken\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box-label\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 700px; top: 40px; color: #42affa; font-size: 50px;\">All Possible States: Balls Shot</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Container for blend mode effect -->\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1500px; height: 880px; isolation: isolate;\">\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"boxneith\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 0px solid #42affa; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .9); border-radius: 10px;mix-blend-mode: normal;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "  <!-- Circle 1 - gray/dimmed -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 200px; width: 700px; height: 700px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border: 0px solid #666666; border-radius: 50%; \"></div>\n",
        "  \n",
        "  <!-- Circle 2 - gray/dimmed -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 850px; top: 350px; width: 240px; height: 240px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border: 0px solid #666666; border-radius: 50%;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; color: black; font-size: 40px; \">$$P(\\text{Target Hit})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 900px; top: 200px; color: black; font-size: 30px;\">$$P(\\text{Shooter Was Broken})$$</div>\n",
        ":::{.clearfragment}\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 950px; top: 720px; color: #051e2eff; font-size: 30px; font-weight: bold; text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px black;\">$$P(\\overline{\\text{Target Hit}} \\cap \\overline{\\text{Shooter Broken}})$$</div>\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "<!-- Slide 4: Understanding Set Space (Given -->\n",
        "## What Can we Identify in our Set? {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "### Probability of Hitting The shot GIVEN the evidence the Shooter is broken\n",
        ":::\n",
        "We need to change our frame of reference\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"box-label\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 700px; top: 40px;  color: #42affa; font-size: 50px;\">All Possible States: Balls Shot</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 200px; width: 700px; height: 700px; background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.3); border: 3px solid #ff6464; border-radius: 50%;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; color: white; font-size: 40px; \">$$P(\\text{Target Hit})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"circle2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 850px; top:350px; width: 240px; height: 240px; background: rgba(100, 255, 100, 0.3); border: 3px solid #64ff64; border-radius: 50%;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label2\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 900px; top: 200px; color: white; font-size: 30px;\">$$P(\\text{Shooter Was Broken})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 5: Understanding Set Space (Part 3 - AND) -->\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "### Probability of Hitting The shot GIVEN the evidence the Shooter is broken\n",
        "By setting our Evidence to true, we shrink the universe of posibility to the subset of P(Shooter Was Broken). \n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"circle2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- <div data-id=\"box-label\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 700px; top: 40px; color: #42affa; font-size: 50px;\">All Possible States: Balls Shot</div> -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Container for blend mode effect -->\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1500px; height: 880px; isolation: isolate;\">\n",
        "  <!-- Circle 1 - darker with blend mode -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 400px; top: 200px; width: 300px; height: 300px; background: rgba(134, 134, 134, 1); border: 0px solid #ff6464; border-radius: 50%; mix-blend-mode: overlay;\"></div>\n",
        "  \n",
        " \n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 150px; top: 550px; color: white; font-size: 40px;\">$$P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cap \\text{Shooter Broken})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label2\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 700px; top: 10px; color: white; font-size: 30px; \">$$P(\\text{Shooter Was Broken})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 5: Understanding Set Space (Part 3 - AND) -->\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "### Probability of Hitting The shot GIVEN the evidence the Shooter is broken\n",
        "Lets define ratios in terms of prior Set \"All Possible States: Balls Shot\"\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"circle2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Container for blend mode effect -->\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1500px; height: 880px; isolation: isolate;\">\n",
        "  <!-- Circle 1 - darker with blend mode -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 400px; top: 200px; width: 300px; height: 300px; background: rgba(134, 134, 134, 1); border: 0px solid #ff6464; border-radius: 50%; mix-blend-mode: overlay;\"></div>\n",
        "  \n",
        " \n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 150px; top: 550px; color: white; font-size: 40px;\">$$P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cap \\text{Shooter Broken})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label2\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 700px; top: 40px; color: white; font-size: 50px; \">$$P(\\text{Shooter Was Broken})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 5: Understanding Set Space (Part 3 - AND) -->\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "### Probability of Hitting The shot GIVEN the evidence the Shooter is broken\n",
        "So what is P(Target Hit | Shooter was broken)?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"circle2\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 100px; top: 100px; width: 1500px; height: 880px; border: 3px solid #42affa; border-radius: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Container for blend mode effect -->\n",
        "<div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1500px; height: 880px; isolation: isolate;\">\n",
        "  <!-- Circle 1 - darker with blend mode -->\n",
        "  <div data-id=\"circle1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 400px; top: 200px; width: 300px; height: 300px; background: rgba(134, 134, 134, 1); border: 0px solid #ff6464; border-radius: 50%; mix-blend-mode: overlay;\"></div>\n",
        "  \n",
        " \n",
        "</div>\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label1\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 150px; top: 550px; color: white; font-size: 40px;\">$$P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cap \\text{Shooter Broken})$$</div>\n",
        "<!-- <div data-id=\"label1prob\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 150px; top: 550px; color: white; font-size: 50px;\">P(Target Hit AND Shooter Was Broken)</div> -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"label2\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 700px; top: 40px; color: white; font-size: 50px; \">$$P(\\text{Shooter Was Broken})$$</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 150px; top: 750px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Target Hit} \\mid \\text{Shooter Broken}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cap \\text{Shooter Broken})}{P(\\text{Shooter Broken})}$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "<!-- Slide 5: Understanding Set Space (Part 3 - AND) -->\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "### Bayes Theorem\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 200px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Target Hit} \\mid \\text{Shooter Broken}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cap \\text{Shooter Broken})}{P(\\text{Shooter Broken})}$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq2\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 350px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Shooter Broken}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cap \\text{Shooter Broken})}{P(\\text{Target Hit} \\mid \\text{Shooter Broken})}$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq3\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 500px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Target Hit} \\cap \\text{Shooter Broken}) = P(\\text{Shooter Broken}) \\times P(\\text{Target Hit} \\mid \\text{Shooter Broken})$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "<!-- Slide 5: Understanding Set Space (Part 3 - AND) -->\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "### Bayes Theorem -- Generally\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 200px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Event} \\mid \\text{Evidence}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Event} \\cap \\text{Evidence})}{P(\\text{Evidence})}$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq2\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 350px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Evidence}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Event} \\cap \\text{Evidence})}{P(\\text{Event} \\mid \\text{Evidence})}$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq3\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 500px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Event} \\cap \\text{Evidence}) = P(\\text{Evidence}) \\times P(\\text{Event} \\mid \\text{Evidence})$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "<!-- Slide 5: Understanding Set Space (Part 3 - AND) -->\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "### Bayes Theorem -- Generally\n",
        "For events that are dependent, finding The intersection (AND) can be difficult. So Bayes tells us =>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq3\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 100px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Evidence} \\cap \\text{Event}) = P(\\text{Event}) \\times P(\\text{Evidence} \\mid \\text{Event})$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eqtext\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 300px; color: white; font-size: 60px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "So we substitute and rewrite the our original equation as:\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq4\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 500px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Event} \\mid \\text{Evidence}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Event}) \\times P(\\text{Evidence} \\mid \\text{Event})}{P(\\text{Evidence})}$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Slide 5: Understanding Set Space (Part 3 - AND) -->\n",
        "## Understanding Set Space {auto-animate=true data-autoslide=\"0\"}\n",
        "### Bayes Theorem -- Generally\n",
        "For events that are dependent, finding The intersection (AND) can be difficult. So Bayes tells us =>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"position: relative; width: 1500px; height: 880px; margin: auto;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"eq4\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 10px; color: white; font-size: 30px; text-align: center; width: 95%;\">\n",
        "$$P(\\text{Event} \\mid \\text{Evidence}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Event}) \\times \\text{Likelihood of this evidence given the event happening}}{P(\\text{Evidence})}$$\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div data-id=\"explanation\" style=\"position: absolute;left: 50px; top: 200px; color: #42affa; font-size: 48px; width: 95%; line-height: 1.4;\">\n",
        "**How Evidence Accumulation Works:**\n",
        "<br><br>\n",
        "• **Start with Prior Belief**: P(Event) - our initial confidence before new evidence \n",
        "<br><br>\n",
        "• **Update with Evidence**: Each new observation becomes \"Evidence,\" and we set up a way of determining if this evidence is likely\n",
        "<br><br>\n",
        "• **Calculate New Confidence**: The posterior P(Event|Evidence) becomes our new prior for the next update\n",
        "<br><br>\n",
        "• **Iterative Process**: Previous posterior → new prior → collect evidence → update → repeat\n",
        "<br><br>\n",
        "This creates a **feedback loop** where reliable evidence strengthens our confidence, while contradictory evidence appropriately weakens it, leading to increasingly accurate beliefs over time.\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Activity: Bayes and the Broken Motor\n",
        "\n",
        "### Setup\n",
        "* **Box A (Good Motor):** 36 Green beads (90%), 4 Red beads (10%)\n",
        "* **Box B (Bad Motor):** 20 Green beads (50%), 20 Red beads (50%)\n",
        "* Student draws a bead from a randomly chosen box.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Scenario\n",
        "Suppose a student draws a **red bead**. What is the probability it came from Box B?\n",
        "\n",
        "### Bayes Calculation\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(\\text{Box B} \\mid \\text{Red}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Red} \\mid \\text{Box B}) \\cdot P(\\text{Box B})}{P(\\text{Red})}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## Activity: Bayes and the Broken Motor\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 1: Priors**  \n",
        "$P(\\text{Box A}) = 0.5$  \n",
        "$P(\\text{Box B}) = 0.5$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 2: Likelihoods**  \n",
        "$P(\\text{Red} \\mid \\text{Box A}) = \\frac{4}{40} = 0.10$  \n",
        "$P(\\text{Red} \\mid \\text{Box B}) = \\frac{20}{40} = 0.50$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 3: Total probability of red bead**  \n",
        "$P(\\text{Red}) = 0.10 \\times 0.5 + 0.50 \\times 0.5 = 0.05 + 0.25 = 0.30$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(\\text{Box B} \\mid \\text{Red}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Red} \\mid \\text{Box B}) \\cdot P(\\text{Box B})}{P(\\text{Red})}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Example Draw Sequences"
      ],
      "id": "97e66e7b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "#| eval: true\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
        "\n",
        "# Likelihoods\n",
        "pRGB = 0.5  # P(Red | Box B)\n",
        "pRGA = 0.1  # P(Red | Box A)\n",
        "pGGB = 0.5  # P(Green | Box B)\n",
        "pGGA = 0.9  # P(Green | Box A)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initial priors\n",
        "pB_init = 0.5\n",
        "pA_init = 0.5\n",
        "\n",
        "sequence1 = [\"r\", \"g\", \"r\", \"g\"]\n",
        "sequence2 = [\"g\", \"g\", \"r\", \"g\", \"r\"]\n",
        "sequence3 = [\"r\", \"r\", \"g\", \"r\", \"g\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "sequences = [\n",
        "    (\"Sequence 1\", sequence1),\n",
        "    (\"Sequence 2\", sequence2),\n",
        "    (\"Sequence 3\", sequence3)\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Process all sequences and store results\n",
        "all_results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for seq_name, sequence in sequences:\n",
        "    pB = pB_init\n",
        "    pA = pA_init\n",
        "    \n",
        "    results = [(\"Initial\", \"-\", round(pB * 100, 1))]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for i, color in enumerate(sequence, 1):\n",
        "        if color == \"r\":\n",
        "            # Red bead drawn\n",
        "            likelihood_A = pRGA\n",
        "            likelihood_B = pRGB\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            # Green bead drawn\n",
        "            likelihood_A = pGGA\n",
        "            likelihood_B = pGGB\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Calculate total probability of observing this color\n",
        "        p_color = likelihood_A * pA + likelihood_B * pB\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Update posteriors using Bayes' theorem\n",
        "        pA = (likelihood_A * pA) / p_color\n",
        "        pB = (likelihood_B * pB) / p_color\n",
        "        \n",
        "        results.append((f\"Draw {i}\", color.upper(), round(pB * 100, 1)))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Create DataFrame for this sequence\n",
        "    df = pd.DataFrame(results, columns=['Step', 'Bead Color', f'P(Box B) % - {seq_name}'])\n",
        "    all_results.append(df)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display in 3 columns using HTML\n",
        "from IPython.display import HTML\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert DataFrames to HTML\n",
        "html_tables = []\n",
        "for df in all_results:\n",
        "    html_table = df.to_html(index=False, table_id=\"bayesian-table\", \n",
        "                           classes=\"table table-striped\",\n",
        "                           escape=False)\n",
        "    html_tables.append(html_table)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create 3-column layout\n",
        "html_output = f\"\"\"\n",
        "<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px;\">\n",
        "    <div style=\"flex: 1;\">{html_tables[0]}</div>\n",
        "    <div style=\"flex: 1;\">{html_tables[1]}</div>\n",
        "    <div style=\"flex: 1;\">{html_tables[2]}</div>\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "display(HTML(html_output))"
      ],
      "id": "3a359bfe",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "raw",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**Notice:** Red beads increase P(Box B), green beads decrease it!\n",
        "\n",
        "---"
      ],
      "id": "41b1c490"
